<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malay Annals</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1612</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Sejarah Melayu, Sulalatus Salatin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Malay Annals are a Malay literary chronicle of the rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a>, tracing them from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sang-nila-utama">Sang Nila Utama</a>'s founding of Singapura to the Portuguese conquest of Malacca in 1511. The best-known version was edited in 1612 at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a>. Mixing legend with history, they are a main source for the early Malay kingdoms and for Malay ideas of kingship.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malay-annals.jpg" alt="Malay Annals" width="245" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frontispiece_of_a_Jawi_edition_of_the_Malay_Annals.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
